<title>UK: Pound hurts SmithKline profits.</title>
<headline>Pound hurts SmithKline profits.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>British-based drugs company SmithKline Beecham Plc said on Tuesday that the strong pound had eaten into its profit advance in the second quarter of the year.</p>
<p>SmithKline said pre-tax profit rose 4.1 percent to 356 million pounds ($595.7 million) from 342 million a year earlier, but sales slipped one percent to 1.9 billion pounds. The figures were below analysts' forecasts for pre-tax profit of between 360 and 382 million pounds.</p>
